// elimination_fine_chain.vo.expected: expected VO derived by hand from doc/formal (ir_vo.tex WF-VO-*, passes.tex
// I1-I5 and the planner O-/S-/R- rules), independently of the producer.
// Every step is preceded by its ordering rule; deterministic tie-breaks are stated below.
// Planner elimination,fine: variable sequence = MCS order a,b,c,d.
// c0=Edge(a,b), c1=Edge(b,c), c2=Edge(d,c)
// H-MCSTie: maximum-cardinality search starts and breaks ties by first written
// variable occurrence. Coarse reverses MCS; Fine uses the forward MCS sequence.
// O-FineVariables: prioritize variables with a connected ready holder, then use
// grouped heuristic variable order (forward MCS for Elimination). O-FineChoice:
// choose a connected holder first, then its fixed heuristic sequence position.
struct OrientedChain ; relation Edge (src : i32 [0] , dst : i32 [0]) ; answer (a , d) : - Edge (a , b) , Edge (b , c) , Edge (d , c) ;
valuation {
    // fineStep(a): only holder c0
    Edge @ 0 (a , _) ;
    // fineStep(b): c0 connected
    Edge @ 0 (a , b) ;
    // introduce(b): check of c1
    Edge @ 1 (b , _) ;
    // fineStep(c): c1 connected
    Edge @ 1 (b , c) ;
    // introduce(c): check of c2
    Edge @ 2 (_ , c) ;
    // fineStep(d): c2; full row
    Edge @ 2 (d , c) ;
}
